    "updated_at": "2026-11-22T19:09:42Z",
    "body": "Looks already fixed on upstream/main 6e641dac7: gpu_probe_and_headless_render_survive_parallel_start passes without a production change. Suggest closing; the maintainer decides.\n\nThe local pin runs the adapter probe and the headless renderer together eight times. It passed in 3.01 seconds. The test command was:\n\n`cargo xtask gate test gpu_probe_and_headless_render_survive_parallel_start --crate camcraft-ui --exact`\n\nThis local result does not prove that the intermittent crash on uma is fixed. I did not run the pin on uma. No known fixing commit was found.\n\nThe failed artifact shows that adapter_probe_names_the_gpu passed before the crash. It contains graphics-device permission warnings. It contains no backtrace or core file. The crashing test remains unknown.\n\nThe same UI library SIGSEGV was reported in #2807 before PR #3363. The GPU seam merge does not establish the cause.\n\nSTOPPED because the pin passes on unchanged production code. No production code changed. No PR was opened. Claim released.\n",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
